   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# X-Ray Scan\n\nA glowing scanner bar sweeps across a device and reveals its white-line internals, with one part marked in red. A built-in phone stands in for the product; a host replaces the .xr-outside and .xr-inside layers with its own exterior and interior pictures.\n\nCategory: graphic-looks. Length: 2.17 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A hardware launch should show what is inside the device: the board, the battery, the chip that matters.\n- One internal part is the story, like a new chip or a bigger battery, and should be singled out in the brand color.\n- The reveal should read as a single clean scanner pass, left to right or top to bottom.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The product should come apart into labelled layers: use exploded-view.\n- The product should be measured and annotated from the outside: use blueprint.\n- The subject should read as a printed poster rather than a device scan: use two-ink-print.\n\nVariables:\n- direction (enum): Direction, default \"horizontal\"\n- shell (color): Shell, default \"#E5322D\"\n- accent (color): Accent part, default \"#E5322D\"\n- line (color): Scan line, default \"#FFFFFF\"\n- background (color): Background, default \"#111111\"\n- speed (number, 0.1-4): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
